  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[6\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(3{x}^{2}-2x)] \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+(3{x}^{2}-2x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1+9{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\cdot (6x-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{36x-12}{9{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(1) & =\\frac{36(1)-12}{9({1}^{4})-12({1}^{3})+4({1}^{2})+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
